  "question": "Can current NLC numeric search or Google Books within-volume number search directly explain the isolated historical 3368 -> 3288 target change?",
  "answer": "No. Current NLC ANY search returns no match for disputed 03368, but it also returns no match for the known-positive current 905s values 03288 and 08643, so numeric no-result behavior cannot establish absence. Google Books SearchWithinVolume2 returns noisy page-token candidates for both 三三六八 and 三二八八, and conflicting title+number queries return the same PP61/PP64 tokens. The three 三二八八 page-token candidates were navigated to the hash-bound 1959 scan and manually reviewed without project OCR at PDF26/PDF28/PDF52; no exact printed 三二八八/3288 appears there. These are false-positive locator hits. The routes are therefore closed as search/index boundaries only; they do not prove global absence of 3288 from the 1959 catalog and do not identify why the target changed from 3368 to 3288.",
